Accurona is an intentionally maintained fork. It is not affiliated with or
endorsed by Mastershort, and "NeonPlan" is not part of its name. Upstream
releases are merged into it on a schedule; nothing from Accurona is proposed
back upstream as a merge.

Upstream's release history up to the fork point (NeonPlan 3D 1.23.1) is kept
as written in CHANGELOG.md and docs/release-*.md.

Furniture packs (.fp3dpack) published by Mastershort remain his work under
the terms he sells or gives them under. Accurona reads them so that packs made
for NeonPlan 3D keep working; it does not redistribute them.

Bundled fonts carry their own licences, next to each font file in
custom_components/accurona/frontend/fonts/.

The Ship-D hull parameterisation in frontend/src/hull/shipd.ts is a
TypeScript port of HullParameterization.py by Noah J. Bagazinski, from
https://github.com/noahbagz/C_ShipGen, used under the MIT License below. The
parameterisation and the Ship-D dataset are described in Bagazinski, N. J. and
Ahmed, F., "Ship-D: Ship Hull Dataset for Design Optimization using Machine
Learning" (2023). The hull vectors in frontend/src/hull/fixtures/shipd.json
come from that dataset (Harvard Dataverse, doi:10.7910/DVN/MMGAUS, CC0 1.0).

